      "text": "This problem can be solved by using the distributive property.\n\nStep 1: Apply the distributive property\nTo expand the product, distribute the terms in the first set of parentheses to both terms in the second set of parentheses:\n\n${(2x+3)(x+5)} = 2x(x) + 2x(5) + 3(x) + 3(5)$\n\nStep 2: Perform the multiplication\nNow, carry out the multiplication for each term:\n\n${2x(x) + 2x(5) + 3(x) + 3(5)} = 2x^{2} + 10x + 3x + 15$\n\nStep 3: Combine like terms\nCombine the terms with the same exponents:\n\n$2x^{2} + 10x + 3x + 15 = 2x^{2} + 13x + 15$\n\nSo, ${(2x+3)(x+5)} = \\boxed{2x^{2} + 13x + 15}$.",
